    "rationale": "Most symbols are best treated as lexical because the suggested surface resemblances do not support compositional paradigms. In particular, P1–P14 are opaque indexed procedures, not P + numeral; start:X/from:X do not show a meaning contrast in the same frame; and other shared substrings like ST-, -ING, -PE, -AP, or al- are accidental or semantically inconsistent. Two small paradigms are defensible: (i) hum1/hum2, where hum contributes 'hum' and 1/2 contribute the tone-count contrast; and (ii) STONE-TRACE/FINGER-TRACE, where TRACE contributes 'trace' and the initial element contributes the instrument. All remaining symbols are left lexical to avoid overanalysis.",
